--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ChatbotPage.tsx is the Helix AI-assistant chat screen. Its PageContainer chrome
is the "Helix" title, the "Ask Helix anything about your Tesla fleet" subtitle,
and a History toggle action. The body is two GlassPanels: GlassPanel1 — the
conversation panel that holds the message log (an empty-state Helix hero +
SuggestedPrompts when there are no messages, else the ChatMessageItem rows) and
the bottom input row (a Textarea + a Send affordance that swaps to a Stop
affordance while a reply is revealing); and GlassPanel2 — the "Helix is thinking…"
indicator shown while a reply is pending. The History action reveals the
SessionList sidebar (the session feed + select / new-chat / rename / delete).

The page's DECLARED data sources (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json record
page:system/Chatbot) are exactly the five useChat* hooks: useChatSessions,
useChatHistory, useSendChatMessage, useRenameChatSession, useDeleteChatSession.
(The optional useAiStream/useAiEnabled LLM-streaming branch — AIChatbotIndicator
/ AIVoiceMode — is NOT among this page's declared data sources; it is a separate
parity surface.) The baseline send (POST /chatbot) returns the full reply, which
a client-side typewriter reveals char-by-char into the assistant bubble.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared KMP data layer (P1/S8) already exists:
io.teslasync.shared.core.presentation.chat.ChatStore over
io.teslasync.shared.core.data.repo.HttpChatRepository — the cross-platform port
of the web useChat domain (chatSessions / chatHistory feeds + sendChatMessage /
renameChatSession / deleteChatSession). The A3 chatbot feature views also exist
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.{sessionlist.SessionList,
chatmessageitem.ChatMessageItem, suggestedprompts.SuggestedPrompts}). This page
binds those — no new networking, no re-implemented endpoints, no row/sidebar
re-draws — exactly as the web page composes its hooks + sub-components.

New files (package io.teslasync.android.system, dir com/teslasync/system/):
  - ChatbotPageModel.kt       Pure model: Registration(ROUTE_ID chatbot, WEB_PATH
                              /chatbot, SLUG ChatbotPage), ConversationPhase enum,
                              ChatbotConversation state, LocalMessageIds (web
                              nextLocalId), ChatMessage.toUiMessage projection,
                              planEditAndResend / planRegenerate (web
                              handleEditAndResend / handleRegenerate truncation),
                              hydrateMessages (web hydration race guards),
                              recordChatbotPageOpened.
  - ChatbotPageGlyphs.kt      Send / Stop(Square) / History line ImageVectors
                              (lucide-equivalents; TeslaGlyphs ships none).
  - ChatbotPageSource.kt      ChatbotPageSource seam (chatStore(scope): ChatStore)
                              + chatbotPageSourceOf(repo) — binds the shared S8
                              store over the injected S7 repository.
  - ChatbotPageViewModel.kt   BaseFeedViewModel; sessionsState (chatSessions ▸
                              asUiState) + conversation (combine(localMessages,
                              historyResource, sending, streaming, sessionId) ▸
                              buildConversation) as StateFlows; submit / coroutine
                              typewriter startReveal / stopStreaming;
                              editAndResend / regenerate; loadSession / startNewSession
                              / rename / delete; retryHistory / refreshSessions;
                              the hydration collector; recordViewOpened.
  - ChatbotPage.kt            Stateful entry (viewModel factory) + stateless
                              ChatbotPageContent: ChatbotHeader (PageTitle +
                              subtitle + History toggle) over ConversationPanel
                              (GlassPanel1: ConversationLog [Spinner / ChatHero /
                              QueryError / MessageList] + divider + ChatInputRow),
                              ThinkingIndicator (GlassPanel2 + TypingDots), and the
                              SessionOverlay (scrim + start-aligned SessionList).
  - ChatbotPageHost.kt        ChatbotRoute() binds chatbotPageSourceOf(
                              HttpChatRepository(container.api, container.cacheStore));
                              ChatbotPageHost.register() -> PageHosts.register("chatbot").

Edits (registration + ledger only):
  - TeslaSyncApplication.kt   import + ChatbotPageHost.register() at process start.
  - apps/parity/android-ledger.json  page:system/Chatbot row (done, 18/18).
  - res/values/strings.xml    NO edit — all 13 translation_chatbot_* keys already
                              present in the generated catalog.

Notes:
  - Scope honesty: the manifest's 5 declared data sources are the useChat* hooks;
    the AI SSE branch (useAiStream/useAiEnabled) is out of this unit's scope and
    is not implemented here. The baseline path exercises all 5 hooks, both
    GlassPanels, and all 13 strings.
  - SI: no chat field is unit-bearing (ids, ISO timestamps, titles, free text) —
    no SI conversion; clock/locale formatting is at the render boundary inside
    ChatMessageItem (S5).
  - States: the sessions feed renders loading / empty / content / error+retry via
    the bound SessionList(state=…); the conversation renders loading (Spinner) /
    empty (Helix hero + SuggestedPrompts) / content (ChatMessageItem list) /
    error (QueryError + retryHistory) from the history feed's UiState.
  - i18n: every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept.
  - a11y: PageTitle heading; conversation log is an aria-live polite region with
    the localized name; Send/Stop carry localized content descriptions; History
    button mirrors aria-pressed via semantics{selected}; ≥48 dp targets via the
    shared Button (ADR-015). Dynamic color + dark theme via MaterialTheme (no
    hardcoded colors, ADR-005).

